// ============================================================================
// lottery-odds.epher -- the 6-of-49 lottery: ticket odds, exactly
//
// A lottery draw picks 6 numbers out of 49, so there are ncr(49, 6) =
// 13983816 equally likely tickets. A fixed ticket with 6 chosen numbers
// matches k of the drawn numbers in ncr(6, k) * ncr(43, 6 - k) ways
// (choose which of your numbers hit, and which of the 43 others fill the
// rest of the draw), so the probabilities are exact rationals:
//
//   P(6 of 6) = 1 / 13983816
//   P(3 of 6) = ncr(6, 3) * ncr(43, 3) / ncr(49, 6) = 246820 / 13983816
//
// The hypergeometric model is the same one used for poker hands; the
// quoted "1 in ..." odds are the reciprocal of each probability.
//
// Source: Feller, "An Introduction to Probability Theory and Its
// Applications", volume 1, chapter 2. Fractions are exact; epher shows
// about 12 digits for the probabilities whose denominator is large.
//
// Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/probability/counting/lottery-odds.epher"
// Web/desktop:             paste the file into the entry, press Enter
// ============================================================================

// ---- results ----
// All possible tickets.
ncr(49, 6)
print("possible tickets:", ncr(49, 6))

// Matching all six drawn numbers: your one combination out of the lot.
print("P(6 of 6):", 1 / ncr(49, 6))
print("jackpot odds: 1 in", ncr(49, 6))

// Matching exactly three: the usual "small prize" event.
print("P(3 of 6):", ncr(6, 3) * ncr(43, 3) / ncr(49, 6))
print("exact fraction: 246820 / 13983816")
print("3-of-6 odds, 1 in:", ncr(49, 6) / (ncr(6, 3) * ncr(43, 3)))

// Matching exactly four, five and six, for the full picture.
print("P(4 of 6):", ncr(6, 4) * ncr(43, 2) / ncr(49, 6))
print("P(5 of 6):", ncr(6, 5) * ncr(43, 1) / ncr(49, 6))

// Every ticket matches 0 to 6 numbers, so the seven probabilities sum to
// 1. The counting version of that identity is Vandermonde's: summing
// ncr(6, k) * ncr(43, 6 - k) over k = 0..6 counts all ncr(49, 6) draws
// by splitting each draw into matches and non-matches of the ticket.
v = {0, 0}
while v[1] < 7 do v = {v[1] + 1, v[2] + ncr(6, v[1]) * ncr(43, 6 - v[1])}
v[2] == ncr(49, 6)
// ---- expected output ----
// = 13983816
// = possible tickets: 13983816
// = P(6 of 6): 0.0000000715112384202
// = jackpot odds: 1 in 13983816
// = P(3 of 6): 0.0176504038669
// = exact fraction: 246820 / 13983816
// = 3-of-6 odds, 1 in: 56.6559273965
// = P(4 of 6): 0.000968619724401
// = P(5 of 6): 0.0000184498995124
// = {0, 0}
// = true
